You can apply the same validation arguments to a body parameter that you would use with `Query`.  
Add `Body` (or `Annotated` + `Body`) to the field and pass the desired limit, e.g.:

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI, Body

app = FastAPI()

@app.post("/items/")
def create_item(
    name: str = Body(..., max_length=50)   # max 50 characters
):
    return {"name": name}
```

`Body` accepts the same extra validation arguments as `Query`, `Path`, etc., so you can set `max_length`, `gt`, `lt`, `ge`, `le`, etc., on body fields [1][2].
